column45:
Agree. I've used "void main(void)" on embedded applications where 1. there is no OS under you.  2.  it can never "exit"<p>void main(void) { 
   init(); 
   for(;;) { 
     web_tick(); 
     serial_tick(); 
     tcp_tick();
     etc.
   }
}<p>An example is the horrible Dynamic C compiler from z-world (or digi as they are now called).  Guys who complain about "violating standards" clearly haven't worked in diverse enough fields on broken, shitty and half-standard compilers ;)
